// Name: SSH Brute Force - Repeated Failed Logins From One Source
// Data source: Linux Syslog (auth/authpriv) via Azure Monitor Agent -> Syslog table
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 Brute Force, T1110.001 Password Guessing (Credential Access)
// Logic: 5 or more "Failed password" lines from one source IP within the rule's 10-minute lookback
// Schedule: runs every 5 minutes, looks back 10 minutes
// Known false positives: a user mistyping a password across several attempts; automation with a stale password
// Known limitations:
//  - rsyslog can collapse repeats into "message repeated N times", so count() may under-count a burst
//  - alerts for the same burst may repeat across overlapping runs (candidate for alert grouping/suppression)
//  - fixed in this version: matching only ProcessName == "sshd" (an earlier version counted sudo lines
//    that contained the text "Failed password"), no bin() window, and the IP pattern now accepts IPv6
Syslog
| where ProcessName == "sshd"
| where SyslogMessage has "Failed password"
| extend SourceIP = extract(@"from (\S+) port", 1, SyslogMessage)
| extend TargetUser = extract(@"Failed password for (?:invalid user )?(\S+) from", 1, SyslogMessage)
| summarize Failures = count(), Users = make_set(TargetUser), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by SourceIP
| where Failures >= 5
